@bank all
// B3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-4; lead 39: no writer seat, the builder writes its own leftovers): M18 Shutdowns
// (24w), the keys the code reads that SW3's m18.lines (claude/p5s5-words) doesn't have. Same style: short labels for the
// phone, plain words. {where}: the branch ("the galley circuit"); {text}: rooms; {thing}: what an hour clashes with;
// {time}: 14:00; {day}: a day number or "tomorrow"; {n}: a count. Keep these keys out of m18.lines (one home each).

// ---- the planning screen: headings and states ----
== sd.none.untrained
- Calder shows you shutdowns once you're a Senior Officer.
== sd.booked.head
- Booked
== sd.booked.open
- settles at 22:00 the evening before
== sd.booked.set
- settled: the crew have planned round it
== sd.settled
- This one's settled: Day {day}, {time}. Be at the junction then.
== sd.step.job
- 1. The job
== sd.step.branch
- 2. The branch to switch off
== sd.step.keep
- 3. Keep power to
== sd.step.hour
- 4. The hour
== sd.step.warn
- 5. Warn who's affected
// toggles: "Keep on: Galley" until pressed, then "Kept on: Galley" (the code adds the space and the room)
== sd.keep.off
- Keep on:
== sd.keep.on
- Kept on:
== sd.hour.bad
- Clashes with {thing}.
== sd.hour.quietest
- Quietest hour
// what an hour clashes with, joined into sd.hour.bad
== sd.mark.breakfast
- breakfast
== sd.mark.dinner
- dinner
== sd.mark.event
- a ship event
== sd.warn.none
- Nobody to warn at that hour.
// beside Brennan's name while he hasn't been told face to face
== sd.warn.brennan
- tell him in person before 22:00
// more than six people: one notice for everyone
== sd.warn.all
- Post a ship notice: warn all {n}
== sd.warn.alldone
- Ship notice posted: all {n} warned.
== sd.notice.title
- Ship notice
== sd.notice.posted
- Posted: power off in {text}, {time}. {n} people warned.
== sd.rebook
- Change the booking
== sd.blocked
- That hour can't be booked. Pick another.
== sd.bad.warn
- You can book it, but people will feel it.
== sd.title
- Shutdown booked
// a warned person's answer (picked by index)
== sd.warn.reply
- Thanks for the warning. I'll work round it.
- Noted. I'll be elsewhere.
- An hour? Fine. Thanks for telling me.

// ---- the job board and the Schedule ----
== sd.why
- needs a shutdown: book one in Works
== sd.why.booked
- shutdown booked: {day}, {time}
== sd.row
- Your shutdown: {where}

// ---- the training, while the booking waits (once a ship hour, Calder) ----
== sd.train.remind
- Your shutdown plan: book it before the shift ends.

// ---- the day: the crew in the branch's rooms, in their bubbles (picked by index) ----
== sd.crew.off
- Lights! Oh, the shutdown.
- There it goes. Right on time.
- Power's off in here. As promised.
== sd.crew.back
- And we're back. Thanks for the warning.
- Lights on. Quick work.
- Back on. Barely noticed.
== sd.crew.grumble
- In the middle of dinner? Really?
- Whose idea was this hour?
- Eating by torchlight. Lovely.

// ---- the parts (RV20's M3): named at booking, in the 22:00 Mail and the morning's notice ({thing}: "a breaker and a bracket") ----
== sd.parts.bring
- Bring {thing}.
== sd.parts.make
- (make the {thing} in the machine shop)
== sd.parts.none
- nothing to fetch
== sd.morning
- Shutdown at {time}, {where}. Take the job now and get {thing} first.
== sd.notice.parts
- You still need {thing}.
// the hour ran out with the power off and the work not done (Calder)
== sd.over
- Hour's up. Power back on: it never stays off past the booking. Finish it on the next one.
